1
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:51,000
The secret lives of animals revealed!

2
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Barnyard is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Steve Oedekerk.

3
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Otis is a mischievous, carefree Holstein cow who lives on a farm where,
unbeknownst to humans, the animals are anthropomorphic.

4
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
He prefers having fun with his best friends: Pip the mouse, Freddy the ferret, Peck the rooster,
and Pig the pig - rather than following strict rules and accepting responsibility.

5
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
This annoys his stern adoptive father Ben, the leader of the farm's community.

6
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
One evening, Otis convinces Ben to cover his night watch so he can attend a massive party in the barn and impress
Daisy, a pregnant cow who recently arrived at the farm with her best friend Bessy as a newcomer.

7
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
As the animals party, Dag the coyote and his pack
attempt to raid the chicken coop.

8
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Ben fends them off alone but is fatally wounded and killed.

9
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Otis must now learn the value of responsibility when he
becomes the leader of his farm home's community.

10
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Otis (voice), played by Kevin James.

11
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Daisy (voice), played by Courteney Cox.

12
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Ben (voice), played by Sam Elliott.

13
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
Miles (voice), played by Danny Glover.

14
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Bessy (voice), played by Wanda Sykes.

15
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Etta (voice), played by Andie MacDowell.

16
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Barnyard (also known as Barnyard: The Original Party Animals) is a 2006
American animated comedy film written and directed by Steve Oedekerk.

17
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
The film features an ensemble cast, including Kevin James, Courteney Cox, Sam
Elliott, Danny Glover, Wanda Sykes, Andie MacDowell and David Koechner.

18
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
It tells the story of Otis, a carefree Holstein cow, who learns the value of responsibility when he becomes
the leader of his farm home's community after his adoptive father's death from a coyote attack.

19
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Barnyard was released in the United States on
August 4, 2006, by Paramount Pictures.

20
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $116.5
million worldwide against a $51 million production budget.

21
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
A sequel television series, Back at the Barnyard, premiered in 2007.

22
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film explores themes of farm, peasant, villain, family, farmer.

23
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The tone is lighthearted.
